* 3 Nov 26 dm  The picker extended (owner, 2 Nov: "Extend the picker"): mode 'list', a pick from a list the caller gives, moved here from $tk_pickrec (S.88 U9) so that the
*              facade is the library again, and given optional columns (headings and widths) and an optional delete action that the CALLER confirms (res 'delete').
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_picker(mode, file, id, res, newtext)
*
*     mode     null: the person picks a file, then a record in it.  'file': only the file (file is the answer, id is null).  'record': file is given
*              and only the record is picked (Esc then ends the picker).
*     file     the file picked (or, with mode 'record', the file to pick in)
*     id       the record id picked, exactly as the file stores it
*     res      'ok' a record (or, with mode 'file', a file) was picked; 'new' the person pressed Ctrl-N in the list of records: file is the file and newtext
*              is what had been typed into the filter, and id is null - the caller then runs ITS OWN new-record path, with its own gates; 'cancel' Esc at the
*              first list, a session with no terminal, no file to pick from, or a file that cannot be opened
*     newtext  see 'new'
*
*   The files are the account's VOC entries of type F (or whose first line begins "File "), leaving out the names that begin with a dollar sign: the list the
*   IDE shows.  The records are listed by $sl_pickwin's paged source, so a file of a million records is read a page at a time.  Esc in the list of records
*   goes back to the list of files.  THE PICKER NEVER WRITES: it opens the file for reading, takes no lock and creates, changes and deletes nothing.  What the
*   caller does with the answer, and whether it may, is the caller's.
*
*   MODE 'LIST' (field 1 of mode): a pick from a LIST THE CALLER GIVES, not from a file.  file = the entries, one to a field (value 1 the name, value 2 a description shown
*   beside it - or, with columns, the column texts as subvalues - and value 3 the help shown on ?); id = the window's title on the way in and the number of the entry chosen
*   (in file) on the way out; newtext = the number of the entry the window starts on, on the way in, and null on the way out.  Typing narrows the list to the entries that
*   hold the text in the name, the description or a column.  Nothing is opened, read or written.  Optional, in the other fields of mode:
*     mode<2>  the column headings, one value to a column, the first for the name (null: no columns, the window as it always was)
*     mode<3>  the column widths, the same way (a width that is not a number is 12)
*     mode<4>  'delete': the Del key ends the window with res 'delete' and id the number of the entry the cursor was on.  THE PICKER DELETES NOTHING: the caller asks its
*              own question (a box with the name typed, say) and deletes, or not; it may open the picker again on the same entry (newtext).
*   res is 'ok' (Enter chose), 'delete' (Del, with mode<4> 'delete', on an entry) or 'cancel' (Esc, a session with no terminal, an empty list).
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_picker(mode, file, id, res, newtext)
$catalog $sl_picker

   if mode<1> = 'list' then
      gosub pick.list
      return
   end

   res = 'cancel'
   id = ''
   newtext = ''
   if system(25) then return                  ;* a phantom has no terminal

   stage = 1
   if mode = 'record' then stage = 2

   loop
      if stage = 1 then
         gosub list.files
         if fl = '' then return
         call $sl_pickwin(fl, sysmsg(12176), 0, 0, pr, ps, '', '')
         if ps # 0 then return
         file = fl<pr, 1>
         if mode = 'file' then
            res = 'ok'
            return
         end
         stage = 2
      end else
         open file to fv else return
         call $sl_pickwin('', sysmsg(12177, file), 0, 0, pr, ps, fv, '0' : @fm : 200 : @fm : 100000 : @fm : 20000, 'ctrl-n', typed)
         close fv
         begin case
            case ps = 0
               id = pr
               res = 'ok'
               return
            case ps = 2
               newtext = typed
               res = 'new'
               return
            case mode = 'record'
               return
            case 1
               stage = 1
         end case
      end
   repeat

   return

* The files of the account, one to a field: the VOC's type F entries (or a description that begins "File "), not the names that begin with a dollar sign
list.files:
   fl = ''
   open 'VOC' to vocf then
      sselect vocf to 9
      readlist ids from 9 else ids = ''
      nid = dcount(ids, @fm)
      if ids = '' then nid = 0
      for i = 1 to nid
         read r from vocf, ids<i> then
            t1 = upcase(r<1>)
            if (t1 = 'F' or t1[1, 5] = 'FILE ') and ids<i>[1, 1] # '$' then fl<-1> = ids<i>
         end
      next i
      close vocf
   end
   return

* Mode 'list': the library's pick window on the caller's entries, one entry chosen (or, with mode<4> 'delete', named for the caller to delete); its number returned
pick.list:
   res = 'cancel'
   ltitle = id
   ldef = newtext
   id = ''
   newtext = ''
   if system(25) or file = '' then return               ;* a phantom has no terminal; an empty list has nothing to choose
   if not(num(ldef)) or ldef < 1 then ldef = 1
   lhot = ''
   if mode<4> = 'delete' then lhot = 'del'
   lcols = ''
   if mode<2> # '' then lcols = mode<2> : @fm : mode<3>
   ltyped = ''
   lcur = ''
   call $sl_pickwin(file, ltitle, 0, ldef, pr, ps, '', '', lhot, ltyped, lcols, lcur)
   begin case
      case ps = 0 and pr > 0
         id = pr
         res = 'ok'
      case ps = 2 and pr = 'del' and lcur > 0
         id = lcur
         res = 'delete'                                    ;* the caller confirms and deletes, or not: nothing is changed here
   end case
   return
end

* END-CODE
